Document source: [PD 002A_2023 Kebijakan dan Kewenangan Pengadaan Barang dan atau Jasa - OCR.pdf](https://365tsel.sharepoint.com/:b:/s/ProcurementAssuranceandComplianceDepartment/IQBX4uYWT53nQbKuEY7RcdXkAaoRs5fhVIgrkSEZuS7iEBI?e=dHoi6j)

Menurut dokumen yang bisa **Procurement Hub Agent** baca, cara menentukan apakah suatu pengadaan masuk kewenangan Kantor Pusat atau Kantor Area dan Regional adalah dengan mencocokkan pengadaan tersebut terhadap kriteria yang diatur dalam Peraturan Direksi Perseroan tentang Kebijakan dan Kewenangan Pengadaan Barang dan/atau Jasa (sebelum Pasal 12):

Kriteria Pengadaan di Kantor Pusat:
- Barang dan/atau Jasa bersifat strategis;
- Barang dan/atau Jasa memerlukan standarisasi, spesifikasi, dan kebijakan Perseroan berskala nasional guna menjamin interoperabilitas, konektifitas, dan kepatuhan terhadap aspek legal dan komersial;
- Barang dan/atau Jasa yang apabila diadakan di Kantor Pusat dapat memberi nilai tambah atau memberikan *economies of scale* bagi Perseroan;
- Barang dan/atau Jasa untuk kebutuhan taktikal dan operasional Kantor Pusat.

Kriteria Pengadaan di Kantor Area dan Regional:
- Barang dan/atau Jasa yang kewenangan, fungsi tugas, dan anggarannya telah dilimpahkan kepada Kantor Area dan Regional sesuai kebijakan Perseroan;
- Barang dan/atau Jasa yang Penyedianya (*Supplier*) bersifat lokal (*localized*) dan lebih efisien bila dilakukan di Area dan Regional;
- Barang dan/atau Jasa untuk kebutuhan taktikal dan operasional Kantor Area dan Regional.

Apabila dibutuhkan pengaturan lebih lanjut mengenai jenis dan kategori Barang dan/atau Jasa yang memenuhi kriteria pengadaan di Kantor Area dan Regional, hal tersebut ditetapkan oleh Pejabat Fungsi Pengadaan tertinggi di bawah Direktur Fungsi Pengadaan di Kantor Pusat sesuai kebutuhan. Selain itu, Fungsi User di Kantor Pusat yang memiliki perpanjangan tangan di Area dan Regional otorisasi kewenangannya mengikuti lokasi dilakukannya transaksi.

Knowledge Level: Level 5 (Others)
Document source: [309 Pengaturan Pelaksanaan Pengadaan Berdasarkan Jenis dan Kategori Barang dan atau Jasa Area_Shared.pdf](https://portal.telkomsel.co.id/FANCY/Homepage)

Based on the documents **Procurement Hub Agent** can access, determining whether a procurement falls under Head Office (*Kantor Pusat*) or Area and Regional authority is evaluated based on specific criteria set out in Pasal 11 (*Kewenangan Pengadaan*):
- Procurement carried out at Head Office (*Kantor Pusat*) covers goods and/or services that:
  - Are strategic in nature;
  - Require standardized specifications and company policies, or involve complex, strategic considerations, and/or legal and commercial impacts;
  - Provide added value or increase economies of scale for the Company if conducted centrally;
  - Fulfill strategic and operational needs of the Head Office.
- Procurement carried out at Area and Regional Offices covers goods and/or services that:
  - Have their authority, function, duties, and budget delegated to the Area and Regional Office in accordance with company policy;
  - Involve localized suppliers and are more efficient if executed at the Area and Regional level;
  - Fulfill tactical and operational needs of the Area and Regional Office.

Knowledge Level: Level 2 (PR)
Document source: [PR 016_2023 - Aktivitas Pengadaan Barang dan-atau jasa (inbound logistics) - OCR.pdf](https://portal.telkomsel.co.id/FANCY/Homepage)

According to the regulations **Procurement Hub Agent** found, the preparation of *Demand Planning* is carried out by the *User* Function and involves other relevant company functions, such as the *Finance Business Partner* Function and the Procurement Function, as set forth in Article 4 (*Pasal 4*) of *Peraturan Direktur* regarding Procurement Activities of Goods and/or Services (*Inbound Logistics*). 

Pursuant to Article 4 paragraph (1), the stages of *Demand Planning* generally comprise the following:
- Ensuring information regarding program approval for Goods and/or Services to be included in the initiative list within the Company's Work Plan and Budget (*Rencana Kerja Anggaran Perseroan* / RKAP) or other required documents;
- Elaborating the detailed requirements for Goods and/or Services down to the *Bill of Quantity* level, *Item* level, or functionality level;
- Checking the availability of existing agreements/contracts (*Perikatan*) for the required Goods and/or Services;
- Approving the list of initiatives in the *Demand Planning*; and
- Verifying the details of the required Goods and/or Services set out in the initiative list to determine whether the process proceeds via *Sourcing* or Purchase Requisition–Purchase Order (PR-PO).

Furthermore, pursuant to Article 4 paragraph (2), the relationship (*keterkaitan*) of *Demand Planning* with other procurement activities is established as follows:
- *Demand Planning* can serve as the foundational information for carrying out *Category Management* activities;
- *Demand Planning* serves as the foundational information for carrying out *Sourcing* activities or contract amendments/variations (*perubahan Perikatan*); and
- *Demand Planning* can serve as the foundational information for conducting *Joint Procurement* activities.

